+## Questions for Chase, answered on the console (cc-P216)
+
+When a Golem needs Chase, the question is on its card on the web console (and on the Shard Console's Golem tab), in
+full, with a button per choice and a box for his own words. His answer goes back to that Golem and it carries on: no
+terminal needed.
+
+**The question** (`questions\<Golem>-P<nn>-<yyyyMMdd-HHmmss>-<4 hex>.json`; `Golem-P<nn>-...` when one Golem works
+alone; `Questions.ps1`, dot-sourced by golem.ps1): the prompt, the whole question, up to four choices (a label and what
+the Golem then does), whether free text is taken, the context (the session's last message or the notification), when
+it was asked, and `irreversible` with why. It is written:
+
+- on **STOPPED** (the Stop hook): from the STOPPED reason, with the choice "Retry with my answer", unless the session
+  asked its own question first;
+- on **NEEDS YOU** (Claude Code's Notification), with "Carry on"; a repeat of the same notification is not a second
+  question, and none is written while a STOPPED prompt's question waits;
+- by the session itself, through **`Ask-Chase.ps1`** (the house rule in every hand-off and in AGENTS.md: "when you must
+  stop for Chase, ask through Ask-Chase.ps1 with choices where you can"), then it ends with `P<nn> STOPPED: asked Chase`:
+
+      powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File D:\UO\golem\Ask-Chase.ps1 -Question "<the whole question>"
+          -Choice "<label>|<what I will then do>" [-Choice2 ... -Choice4 ...] [-NoText] [-Context "..."] [-Irreversible]
+
+  (`-File` cannot pass a list, hence `-Choice2`..`-Choice4`.) The question carries the session's Golem (GOLEM_NAME)
+  and running prompt; Chase is emailed with it.
+
+A question about something that **cannot be undone** (deleting or overwriting saves or data, the LIVE shard or what
+players get, pushing or rewriting main by hand) says so on the card in red and the page asks a confirm
+(`Get-IrreversibleWhy` reads the question and its choices; `-Irreversible` sets it too). A question closes by itself
+when what it asked about goes (`Sync-GolemQuestions`, from every status write): Retry stopped prompt, an answer typed in
+the terminal (the activity that clears NEEDS YOU or STOPPED), the start phrase, parking. The newest ten closed questions
+per Golem are kept, five shown as the card's history with their answers.
+
+**The answer** (`answers\<same id>.json`: who, when, the source, the choice, the words, delivered or not):
+
+- **One way in, whatever the source:** `Submit-GolemAnswer` (Questions.ps1) checks the answer against the question (open,
+  a real choice, words only where taken, at most 2000 characters), creates the answer file once (a second answer, or one
+  to a closed question, is refused: a stale page cannot answer) and closes the question. `Answer-Question.ps1 -Id <id>
+  [-Choice n] [-TextB64 <base64 of UTF-8>] -Who <login> -Source console|shard-console|remote|email|terminal` runs it
+  and then resumes the Golem. P149's email replies are one more source: parse the email, then call this.
+- **Resume** (`golem.ps1 -Event Answer -Question <id>`): a STOPPED prompt goes back first in the queue (Retry stopped
+  prompt's own code, `Invoke-RetryStoppedCore`) and a session is woken on its own model; NEEDS YOU is cleared and a
+  session is woken to carry on with the running prompt. An answer that arrives while the asking session is still
+  running is kept; its STOPPED then retries at once.
+- **The new session reads it first:** the hand-off (or "carry on with it") gives it the answer file's path, what it
+  asked, Chase's choice and words, said to be data from Chase, not a command; the answer is then marked delivered.
+- **Answer text is data:** it travels as base64 on every command line (the web console, the Shard Console, the remote
+  agent) and is never put in a shell, a parameter name or the action log (only its length is).
+
+**The consoles:** the web console's Golem cards show the open questions (newest first) with their choices, the box, the
+context under "What the Golem saw", and "Earlier questions"; the Golem tab's header counts every Golem's open questions;
+one Golem alone gets a "Questions for you" card. `POST /api/answer` has the buttons' own checks (tailnet listener, the
+sidecar's proof, Chase's login, the `X-UOConsole-Action` header, same origin); this PC's own page stays read only. The
+Shard Console lists the open questions on the Golem tab and has **Answer a Golem's question** (a picker, the words, then
+the phrase `answer <golem> <prompt>`; it runs Answer-Question.ps1, and `Test-PlanSafety` holds its arguments to that
+shape).
+
+**Remote Golems:** the agent posts its Golem's questions (`POST /api/agent/questions`, kept in
+`remote\<name>\questions.json`) when they change and every 5 minutes; an answer from the page is queued for the agent
+(`answer` on its allowlist: `Answer-Question.ps1 -Source remote`), which writes the answer file there at its next poll
+and resumes the Golem; the card shows "answer sent" until then.
+
